1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,320
This first improvement is starting to show.

2
00:00:02,320 --> 00:00:05,160
Honestly, whatever the case, to be safe it
should be watching.

3
00:00:05,160 --> 00:00:07,680
I wouldn't dare. I wouldn't dare.

4
00:00:07,680 --> 00:00:08,680
So how do you tell whether it drives well?

5
00:00:08,680 --> 00:00:10,680
It's whether it matches an experienced
driver's intent.

6
00:00:10,680 --> 00:00:11,200
Right.

7
00:00:11,200 --> 00:00:13,120
If it matches your own intent, then it's
driving well.

8
00:00:13,120 --> 00:00:14,680
Not bad.

9
00:00:15,360 --> 00:00:18,840
And this slowdown isn't an instant stop in
the wrong place. It's comfortable.

10
00:00:18,840 --> 00:00:20,640
You can feel it watching and thinking as it
goes.

11
00:00:20,640 --> 00:00:21,440
Exactly.

12
00:00:21,440 --> 00:00:23,560
You can see that once it moved over, it
picked up speed.

13
00:00:25,080 --> 00:00:30,640
Hello everyone, I'm MotorGogo's driver.
Welcome to our brand-new series: MotorTaxi.

14
00:00:30,640 --> 00:00:34,636
As the name suggests, it's a series about
experiencing assisted driving.

15
00:00:34,636 --> 00:00:37,800
But unlike other videos, the route is chosen
by the user.

16
00:00:37,800 --> 00:00:45,560
Today we've invited our second guest:
Robert.

17
00:00:45,560 --> 00:00:50,280
Robert is an old friend and a veteran XPeng
owner.

18
00:00:50,280 --> 00:00:53,840
I have two XPengs: the first an old P7 I
bought in 2021, the second a P7+.

19
00:00:53,840 --> 00:00:55,440
Nearly five years as an owner.

20
00:00:55,440 --> 00:01:00,400
The car we're testing today is this MONA M03
beside us.

21
00:01:00,400 --> 00:01:03,941
It's a single-Turing car running the XOS
6.3.0 distilled version,

22
00:01:03,941 --> 00:01:06,720
and we've brought Robert along to see how it
feels.

23
00:01:10,200 --> 00:01:15,080
I bought my car in July 2021, and back then
there wasn't much choice.

24
00:01:15,080 --> 00:01:22,120
In 2021 there were only a few cars I could
buy — the XPeng P7 among them.

25
00:01:22,120 --> 00:01:25,774
The others you basically couldn't go for.

26
00:01:25,774 --> 00:01:33,440
I genuinely felt the assisted driving would
help me, and that's why I bought this car.

27
00:01:33,440 --> 00:01:43,480
From 2021 to 2024 I drove nearly 100,000 km,
and over 20,000 of those on LCC.

28
00:01:43,480 --> 00:01:50,380
Back then I'd often talk about it in the
owners' group chat — 'LCC has improved

29
00:01:50,380 --> 00:01:56,320
again, it can get through this curve now'.
It was quite interesting.

30
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:06,720
There's a change here now: the speed
transitions are much better than dual-Orin.

31
00:02:06,720 --> 00:02:07,720
It's not as rough, is it?

32
00:02:07,720 --> 00:02:09,840
With dual-Orin it's like this — take this
speed change:

33
00:02:09,840 --> 00:02:16,560
You just said 70 — here it has to drop to
about 30, and it gets very slow.

34
00:02:16,560 --> 00:02:18,142
The feel is just bad.

35
00:02:18,142 --> 00:02:19,800
Yes, the feel is poor.

36
00:02:19,800 --> 00:02:23,249
Just now it clearly came down gradually.

37
00:02:23,249 --> 00:02:28,680
This is just normal driving — and that's the
first improvement.

38
00:02:28,680 --> 00:02:31,480
Now you can see it. Very relaxed.

39
00:02:31,480 --> 00:02:36,080
On a road like this the first thing is speed
control. It matters a lot.

40
00:02:36,080 --> 00:02:40,787
Do you think it recognised the speed bump
there?

41
00:02:40,787 --> 00:02:42,160
Feels like it.

42
00:02:42,160 --> 00:02:43,201
Zoom in a bit.

43
00:02:43,201 --> 00:02:49,520
That action looks like it — and not because
of that car, because it had already gone.

44
00:02:49,520 --> 00:02:54,000
That's a nice surprise. It means the feature
hasn't been cut.

45
00:02:54,000 --> 00:02:59,360
With oncoming traffic it eases out and
waits, so the speed control is very good.

46
00:02:59,360 --> 00:03:07,000
Look, it just keeps slowly creeping along.

47
00:03:07,000 --> 00:03:12,560
There's an oncoming car too, and it moved
over to avoid it first.

48
00:03:12,560 --> 00:03:15,973
How do you judge whether it drives well?

49
00:03:15,973 --> 00:03:20,240
Whether it matches an experienced driver's
intent.

50
00:03:20,240 --> 00:03:22,669
If it matches your intent, then it's driving
well.

51
00:03:22,669 --> 00:03:22,960
Right.

52
00:03:27,360 --> 00:03:29,920
Not bad.

53
00:03:29,920 --> 00:03:35,200
And the slowdown isn't an instant stop
either. It's comfortable.

54
00:03:35,200 --> 00:03:40,600
Here — I still think this is a bit complex,
because the lane is completely blocked.

55
00:03:40,600 --> 00:03:42,109
Let's see how it judges.

56
00:03:42,109 --> 00:03:44,246
I reckon it might need a takeover,

57
00:03:44,246 --> 00:03:47,640
because only the oncoming lane is left —
ours is gone.

58
00:03:47,640 --> 00:03:52,240
Give it a bit of throttle and it follows. It
can follow.

59
00:03:52,240 --> 00:03:58,216
I'm not holding it now, and it came back —
it probably judged it couldn't,

60
00:03:58,216 --> 00:04:00,720
because it's all oncoming lane.

61
00:04:00,720 --> 00:04:01,640
I'll push it along.

62
00:04:01,640 --> 00:04:06,680
If I push it, it judges correctly. Let's try
again — I'll let go.

63
00:04:06,680 --> 00:04:10,120
It's back. It came back on its own. And we
took over again.

64
00:04:15,040 --> 00:04:22,421
This time it reacted fast — as soon as it
knew the Audi had moved right, it set off.

65
00:04:22,421 --> 00:04:26,200
Left turns feel much better than dual-Orin.

66
00:04:26,200 --> 00:04:29,487
It doesn't drive fast here,

67
00:04:29,487 --> 00:04:37,400
and you can't — but its judgement of
vehicles is fairly accurate.

68
00:04:37,400 --> 00:04:41,182
Driving this road isn't especially
comfortable,

69
00:04:41,182 --> 00:04:44,160
because it's very close to the posts.

70
00:04:44,160 --> 00:04:46,470
It isn't that smooth.

71
00:04:46,470 --> 00:04:48,560
It could clip them.

72
00:04:48,560 --> 00:04:53,800
Here you can feel that how it judges the
available space matters.

73
00:04:53,800 --> 00:04:55,678
And it will pull over and stop.

74
00:04:55,678 --> 00:04:55,920
Yes.

75
00:04:58,440 --> 00:05:03,080
'Switching route for you' — and as soon as
it switched, it went.

76
00:05:03,080 --> 00:05:11,572
That's good too, another improvement: it
pulls over to the roadside itself,

77
00:05:11,572 --> 00:05:17,120
and after a route switch it recovers
immediately.

78
00:05:17,120 --> 00:05:19,200
It should edge over.

79
00:05:22,760 --> 00:05:29,466
Could it recognise this speed bump? Did it?

80
00:05:29,466 --> 00:05:31,805
I think it did.

81
00:05:31,805 --> 00:05:33,520
Same as me.

82
00:05:40,000 --> 00:05:44,085
This gap and the narrow one earlier feel
about the same.

83
00:05:44,085 --> 00:05:44,376
Yes.

84
00:05:44,376 --> 00:05:44,960
Strange.

85
00:05:48,120 --> 00:05:55,932
Keep going — that car at the roadside braked
hard. It stopped dead, right?

86
00:05:55,932 --> 00:06:03,427
That deceleration was very quick, the
response fast, and fairly linear.

87
00:06:03,427 --> 00:06:05,960
Any problem? No problem.

88
00:06:05,960 --> 00:06:16,920
Then go. There's one opposite — did it see
it? No problem. Creep along, come across.

89
00:06:16,920 --> 00:06:22,843
But there's a car blocking the way ahead.
It's seen it now.

90
00:06:22,843 --> 00:06:30,574
It's thinking whether to come over or go
straight through. Wait — hazards on.

91
00:06:30,574 --> 00:06:32,080
It's reversing.

92
00:06:32,080 --> 00:06:35,973
What does that show? Its vision reaches a
long way.

93
00:06:35,973 --> 00:06:40,400
Yes — you can see that far, and you can see
its intention.

94
00:06:40,400 --> 00:06:47,933
It seems to prompt for whatever it sees.
That was handled well — it kept watching it.

95
00:06:47,933 --> 00:06:49,440
Yes, watching it.

96
00:06:49,440 --> 00:06:57,429
It can prompt about whatever it sees. Once
the car went in, did it start prompting?

97
00:06:57,429 --> 00:06:58,680
OK, let's go.

98
00:06:58,680 --> 00:07:02,519
Has it seen something else? Another car
ahead?

99
00:07:02,519 --> 00:07:07,360
Ah, it's reacted. There's a car ahead. It
can come across.

100
00:07:08,560 --> 00:07:11,329
It'll be slower — slower than dual-Turing.

101
00:07:11,329 --> 00:07:12,120
Yes, slower.

102
00:07:17,440 --> 00:07:20,548
At least its thinking is on the right track.

103
00:07:20,548 --> 00:07:20,830
Yes.

104
00:07:20,830 --> 00:07:21,960
It's coming out.

105
00:07:26,040 --> 00:07:28,791
OK, you can feel it watching and thinking.

106
00:07:28,791 --> 00:07:29,315
Exactly.

107
00:07:29,315 --> 00:07:32,720
Once it moved over it started prompting —
same here.

108
00:07:42,960 --> 00:07:47,080
There's no way it's letting that one
through. Come on out, get going.

109
00:07:51,240 --> 00:07:54,889
This road is quite a challenge, I think.

110
00:07:54,889 --> 00:07:56,440
Very challenging.

111
00:07:57,600 --> 00:08:02,093
Look — you come out and it's like this
again. I wouldn't know which way to go.

112
00:08:02,093 --> 00:08:06,240
We're going straight, this lane turns left,
and there's a traffic light.

113
00:08:08,640 --> 00:08:13,143
We've been at this for over an hour now, and
the route is genuinely difficult.

114
00:08:13,143 --> 00:08:14,760
Robert, tell us how it felt.

115
00:08:14,760 --> 00:08:19,415
We drove about 40 minutes to get to my
route,

116
00:08:19,415 --> 00:08:28,000
then about 20 minutes on the route I chose.
First the good points — on big roads...

117
00:08:28,000 --> 00:08:31,560
There are a few ways it's better than
dual-Orin.

118
00:08:31,560 --> 00:08:32,005
First:

119
00:08:32,005 --> 00:08:35,714
on main-to-auxiliary road transitions it no
longer

120
00:08:35,714 --> 00:08:39,200
forces a speed reduction the way dual-Orin
did.

121
00:08:39,200 --> 00:08:43,205
Second: with illegally parked cars,
especially when turning right,

122
00:08:43,205 --> 00:08:45,025
its judgement is more precise.

123
00:08:45,025 --> 00:08:49,273
It no longer does what it used to — knowing
there's a parked car ahead

124
00:08:49,273 --> 00:08:53,520
and still pulling over before changing
lanes. Not that stupid anymore.

125
00:08:53,520 --> 00:08:59,920
Third, and I think the biggest change:
overall, big roads and small roads alike,

126
00:08:59,920 --> 00:09:06,480
the driving quality — the smoothness and the
feel — is much better than dual-Orin.

127
00:09:06,480 --> 00:09:07,832
That's the good.

128
00:09:07,832 --> 00:09:11,721
The not-so-good: on small roads, narrow
roads,

129
00:09:11,721 --> 00:09:15,440
it clearly hesitates and won't push forward.

130
00:09:15,440 --> 00:09:15,928
Second,

131
00:09:15,928 --> 00:09:21,650
when meeting oncoming traffic it has no real
ability to get itself out of trouble.

132
00:09:21,650 --> 00:09:26,324
On a narrow road, if a car comes the other
way after we've gone in,

133
00:09:26,324 --> 00:09:30,720
a human would reverse — it can't, so it just
has to keep going.

134
00:09:30,720 --> 00:09:34,280
Roughly the good and the bad — those two big
areas.

135
00:09:34,280 --> 00:09:38,589
In several scenes just now you could clearly
see it thinking — including

136
00:09:38,589 --> 00:09:42,360
when we met the truck reversing, it was
visibly thinking there.

137
00:09:42,360 --> 00:09:44,160
But this version has one problem:

138
00:09:44,160 --> 00:09:47,160
on narrow roads it really isn't as good as
dual-Turing.

139
00:09:47,160 --> 00:09:49,996
The compute isn't enough, so its thinking is
slower.

140
00:09:49,996 --> 00:09:54,360
Otherwise — control, route selection —
basically no difference from dual-Turing.

141
00:09:54,360 --> 00:09:55,735
OK, that's this episode.

142
00:09:55,735 --> 00:09:59,916
This is our first MotorTaxi — tell us in the
comments where you'd like us

143
00:09:59,916 --> 00:10:04,040
to go next and we'll try to meet your
request. That's it for this video.

144
00:10:04,040 --> 00:10:04,600
Thanks, Robert.

145
00:10:04,600 --> 00:10:06,582
Thank you, cameraman.

146
00:10:06,582 --> 00:10:06,960
Bye.
